<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>3.2.3.3 Completing the square exercises 2</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Solve the equation \[ {@ex@} = 0 \] by completing the square. Give exact answers in the form [a,b].</p>
<div>\(x \in \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>To complete the square when the coefficient of \(x^2\) is not 1, first <strong>divide every term by that coefficient</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>Step 1.</strong> Move the constant term to the right-hand side: \({@aa*x^2+bb*x@} = {@-cc@}\).</p>
<p><strong>Step 2.</strong> Divide by \({@aa@}\): \({@x^2+bb/aa*x@} = {@-cc/aa@}\).</p>
<p><strong>Step 3.</strong> Half the coefficient of \(x\) is \({@hh@}\). Add \(\left({@hh@}\right)^2 = {@hh^2@}\) to both sides:</p>
\[ {@x^2+bb/aa*x@} + {@hh^2@} = {@-cc/aa@} + {@hh^2@}, \qquad\text{so}\qquad {@(x+hh)^2@} = {@rhs1@}. \]
<p><strong>Step 4.</strong> Take the square root of both sides: \({@x+hh@} = \pm {@sq@}\).</p>
<p><strong>Step 5.</strong> Solve for \(x\): \(x = {@-hh@} + {@sq@} = {@-hh+sq@}\) or \(x = {@-hh@} - {@sq@} = {@-hh-sq@}\).</p>
<p>Check: substituting each value into \({@ex@}\) gives \(0\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
